# What the install job installs to run the tests on the Pythons that are past their end of life
# (ci.yml): 3.8, 3.9 and 3.10 for now.
#
# This is a COMPLETE lock. Compiled with the oldest Python the package supports (3.8), it holds
# the right version of every package for every Python from 3.8 up, 3.11 to 3.14 included, with
# markers that say which applies where (pytest 8.3.5 on 3.8, 8.4.2 on 3.9, 9.1.1 from 3.10).
# Which Pythons use it is decided by the matrix in ci.yml, not by this file. So retiring a Python
# to it never changes this lock, only ci.yml and the --python-version of the live lock in
# update.sh. And a lock must never be copied into this folder: the live one only covers the
# Pythons it was compiled for, and the entries of the older ones would be lost.
#
# Dependabot cannot maintain a lock like this one: it takes one of the versions of a package as
# "the current one", then checks that the newest can be pinned for every Python the lock covers,
# which cannot be (pytest 9 needs Python 3.10 or later), and reports an error. So this folder
# is not one of its own (see dependabot.yml), and it is next to .github/requirements/ rather than
# inside it: Dependabot also fetches the subfolders of the folder it is given, and it did
# fetch this lock from there, tried to bump its Python 3.9 pins, and failed.
# `bash .github/requirements/update.sh --upgrade` refreshes it when that is worth it: uv gives
# each Python the newest version it supports.
#
# setuptools is here for the tests of the tools that build EnBiD (src/_build_utils.py): they import
# setuptools and distutils, which a Python from 3.12 on does not come with. Without it they are skipped.
pytest
pytest-cov
setuptools
